# evidence-for: US-006, AC-023, AC-024, FR-019, FR-039, AC-039
#
# D-149. `python_project`'s docstring in tests/test_survey.py located the guard
# the FastAPI/Flask decorator pass runs under as "the one immediately below the
# `PY_DECORATOR` and `FLASK_METHODS` patterns". Section 3 measures that clause
# at three revisions: it was true at 1ea2cab, the commit section 4 shows wrote
# it -- FLASK_METHODS at 189 and the guard at 191, two lines apart with nothing
# between -- and stopped being true at e4e0775, the commit that defined
# `call_depth_delta` between them. At this commit the gap is 35 lines and the
# function fills it, so "immediately" named a distance the file no longer has.
#
# Every clause of the rewritten sentence, and where this log measures it:
#   "the first one below the `PY_DECORATOR`     section 2: the patterns are at
#    and `FLASK_METHODS` patterns"              228/233/237 and the guards at
#                                               163, 272 and 697, so the first
#                                               guard below them is 272
#   "which is the guard that pass sits under"   section 1: the guard at 272
#                                               covers 272-334, and all three
#                                               of the decorator pass's use
#                                               sites -- PY_DECORATOR_OPEN.match
#                                               at 278, PY_DECORATOR.search at
#                                               294, FLASK_METHODS.search at
#                                               315 -- fall inside it
#   "not either of the two other guards         section 1: there are exactly
#    spelled the same way"                      three such guards, so two others
#   "was true of the file it was written        section 3, rows 1ea2cab and
#    against"                                   20b15d1: gap 2, nothing between
#   "stopped being true when                    section 3, row e4e0775, and
#    `call_depth_delta` was defined between     section 4: e4e0775 is the commit
#    the patterns and the guard"                that defined it
#
# The sentence now carries two handles on the same guard, one positional and
# one semantic, which is why the second paragraph says so: an insertion between
# the patterns and the guard costs the first handle and leaves the second
# standing, and this defect is what that costs when there is only one handle.
# Section 6 is the residual check -- the only two `immediately` left in the two
# modules are this docstring quoting the retired clause and one at :921 about
# what a regex requires after `detail=`, which is adjacency in a pattern rather
# than a position in a file.
#
# scripts/survey.py is not touched by this commit; the diff is docstrings in
# tests/test_survey.py. See evidence/casting-4-tests-green.log.
#
